    "description": "Mixed Lot Loose Gemstones Ruby Emerald Amethyst Garnet Citrine Aquamarine\nThis lot contains a variety of loose gemstones suitable for jewelry making or collecting. Included are faceted and cabochon stones such as rubies, emeralds, amethysts, garnets, citrines, aquamarines, and other colored and clear varieties. Some stones are branded with JTV and have model numbers including RBP029 (Burma ruby), DLT004 (Diamonella simulated diamond), and Q4E087 (rutilated quartz). The gemstones come in multiple shapes including oval, round, pear, and square. The stones are presented both loose and in boxes. All gemstones appear new or unused with no visible wear or damage. We do not believe all of the gems are authentic and advise to purchase with precaution knowing this. Some imitation gems are present along with other quality gems and we suggest purchasing for collection purposes.\nDisclaimers: Item(s) may show some slight wear from previous use.\nGeneral polishing/cleaning is recommended before use. Item(s) are Thermo Scientific Niton DXL Precious Metal Analyzer tested. The Thermo Scientific Niton DXL desktop x-ray lab delivers fast and accurate XRF-based precious metal analysis. Gems are tested using a Presidium Gem Tester. All items are USED unless otherwise noted. All items are sold AS FOUND. We describe our items to the best of our ability. We are NOT experts in any field.\nCustomer Service:\nOur Customer Service Department is accessible via the Contact Us link above. Our hours of operation are 8:00am-4:30pm CT Monday - Friday. If you have any questions or experience any issues with your order and need assistance, please reach out to us through the Shopgoodwill Customer Service ticketing system rather than calling or sending an email. This allows both parties to have record of conversations as well as an easy reference tool if needed. We strive to respond to any and all customer service tickets within one business day.",
